</style><h2>BlinkyBot 0.2.2</h2><ul><li><strong>Default bots use a signed-in CLI.</strong> BlinkyBot searches a GUI-safe PATH, including <code>/opt/homebrew/bin</code>, <code>~/.local/bin</code>, <code>~/.kimi-code/bin</code>, <code>~/.grok/bin</code>, npm global bins, and nvm version bins, and points the default bots at an installed, signed-in backend. Codex, Claude Code, Kimi Code, and Grok come before OpenCode, then the other agent CLIs, then an API key.</li><li><strong>A missing CLI explains itself.</strong> When nothing is signed in, the chat says so and links to Settings → Backends instead of showing <code>spawn opencode ENOENT</code>.</li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/harrisliangsu/blinky-bot/releases/tag/v0.2.2">Release notes on GitHub</a></p>]]></description>
